@[expose] public section

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

/-
# Problem Description

Formalization of Lemma 18.33.11 (Stacks Tag 04BR), in the chapter "Modules on
Sites", Section 18.33 "Modules of differentials".

Given a commutative diagram of morphisms of *ringed topoi*
```
        f
   X' -----> X
   |         |
   v         v
   Y' -----> Y
```
the universal property of the sheaf module of differentials produces a canonical
comparison map `c_f : f^* Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}` and its adjoint transpose
`c'_f : Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}`.

This file works with *genuine sheaves on sites* (Grothendieck topologies):
sheaves of commutative rings (`Sheaf J CommRingCat`), genuine sheaves of modules
(Mathlib's `SheafOfModules`), and the genuine sheaf-level pushforward / pullback
adjunction `SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction` along a continuous
functor of sites.

## On the formalization of the module of differentials

Mathlib provides modules of differentials and derivations only at the level of
*presheaves of modules* (`PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation`,
`PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.DifferentialsConstruction.relativeDifferentials'`).  There is
currently no sheaf-level module of differentials in Mathlib.

Following the Stacks project, the sheaf module of differentials `Ω_{X/Y}` is
*defined* (Tags 04BL, 04BN) as the sheaf of modules representing the functor of
`Y`-derivations: it comes equipped with a universal `Y`-derivation `d_{X/Y}`
through which every `Y`-derivation factors uniquely.  We package exactly this
data (a genuine `SheafOfModules` together with the universal property of its
universal `Y`-derivation) in the structure `RelativeDifferentials` below.  This
is faithful to the Stacks definition: there `Ω_{X/Y}` *is* by definition the
representing object.

A `Y`-derivation `O_X → F` of a genuine sheaf of modules `F` is, by definition,
a `PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation'` of the underlying presheaf of modules `F.val`
(relative to `g♯ : g⁻¹O_Y ⟶ O_X`); since `F` is a sheaf, this is the genuine
sheaf-theoretic notion of derivation (Tag 04BK).

## Background (Stacks Tags 04BK, 04BL, 04BN, 04BQ)

* For a homomorphism `φ : O₁ ⟶ O₂` of sheaves of rings on a site and an
  `O₂`-module `F`, a `φ`-derivation `D : O₂ ⟶ F` is an additive map of sheaves
  of abelian groups annihilating the image of `φ` (`D ∘ φ = 0`) and satisfying
  the Leibniz rule `D (a b) = a • D b + b • D a` (Tag 04BK).
* The functor `F ↦ Der_{O₁}(O₂, F)` is representable by the sheaf module of
  differentials `Ω_{O₂/O₁}` with universal derivation `d : O₂ ⟶ Ω_{O₂/O₁}`
  (Tags 04BL, 04BN): composition with `d` gives a bijection
  `Hom_{O₂}(Ω_{O₂/O₁}, F) ≃ Der_{O₁}(O₂, F)`, and `Ω_{O₂/O₁}` is generated by
  the `d f`.
* For a morphism of ringed topoi `g : X ⟶ Y`, a `Y`-derivation on an
  `O_X`-module is a `g♯`-derivation, and `Ω_{X/Y} := Ω_{O_X / g⁻¹O_Y}` is the
  corresponding sheaf module of differentials with universal `Y`-derivation
  `d_{X/Y}` (Tag 04BQ).

## Notes / conventions

* Notational abuse in the source (corrected here): the well-typed
  characterizing equation of Statement 3 is
  `c_f ∘ (f^* d_{X/Y}(t)) = d_{X'/Y'} ∘ (f^* t)` as maps `f⁻¹ h_U^# ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}`,
  which is equivalent to `c'_f ∘ d_{X/Y} = D` via the adjunction transpose.
-/

open CategoryTheory PresheafOfModules

namespace Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials

universe v u

/-- The underlying `RingCat`-valued sheaf of a sheaf of commutative rings `O`,
namely the composite with `forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat`.  Genuine sheaves of
`O`-modules are `SheafOfModules` over this. -/
noncomputable abbrev ringSheaf {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
    (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}) : Sheaf J RingCat.{u} :=
  (sheafCompose J (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})).obj O

/-- The `CommRingCat`-valued presheaf of rings `O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat`
underlying the structure sheaf, regarded as a presheaf of rings; this is what
`PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation'` is taken relative to. -/
abbrev ringPsh {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}) :
    Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}

/-!
## Main Definition(s)

We package the data of a ringed topos `X` over a base `Y` together with its
sheaf module of differentials `Ω_{X/Y}` and the universal property of its
universal `Y`-derivation `d_{X/Y}` (Stacks Tags 04BQ, 04BL, 04BN).
-/

-- checkUnivs false positive: `u`, `v` are used separately by the bundled fields
-- (`C : Type u`, `[Category.{v} C]`) but occur only together in the structure's sort.
set_option linter.checkUnivs false in
/-- A **ringed topos over a base**, with its sheaf module of differentials
(Stacks Tags 04BQ, 04BL, 04BN).  The data consists of:

* a site `(C, J)` (a category with a Grothendieck topology) — the topos
  `Sh(C) = Sh(C, J)`;
* a genuine sheaf of commutative rings `O : Sheaf J CommRingCat` — the structure
  sheaf `O_X`;
* the inverse-image structure sheaf `OY : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat` of the base
  (`OY = g⁻¹ O_Y`) together with the structure map `φ : OY ⟶ O.val`
  (`φ = g♯`) of the morphism `g : X ⟶ Y` of ringed topoi;
* the **sheaf module of differentials** `Ω : SheafOfModules` (a genuine sheaf of
  `O`-modules), with its **universal `Y`-derivation** `d`, a derivation of
  sheaves of abelian groups `O_X ⟶ Ω` relative to `φ` (Tag 04BK);
* the universal property `universal` witnessing that `d` is universal among
  `Y`-derivations (Tag 04BN), which is precisely the Stacks definition (Tag
  04BL) of `Ω_{X/Y}` as the representing object of the derivation functor.

A `Y`-derivation `O_X ⟶ F` into a sheaf of modules `F` is encoded as a
`PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation'` of the underlying presheaf of modules `F.val`
relative to `φ`; because `F` is a sheaf, this is the genuine sheaf-theoretic
notion of `Y`-derivation. -/
structure RingedToposOverBase where
  /-- The site underlying the topos `Sh(C_X)`. -/
  {C : Type u}
  /-- Category instance on the site. -/
  [cat : Category.{v} C]
  /-- The Grothendieck topology defining the topos. -/
  J : GrothendieckTopology C
  /-- Composition of sheaves along `forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat` is a sheaf
  (needed to view a sheaf of commutative rings as a sheaf of rings). -/
  [hsc : J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  /-- The structure sheaf of commutative rings `O_X`. -/
  O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}
  /-- The inverse-image structure sheaf of the base, `g⁻¹ O_Y`, as a presheaf of
  commutative rings on `C`. -/
  OY : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}
  /-- The structure map `g♯ : g⁻¹ O_Y ⟶ O_X` of the morphism `g : X ⟶ Y`. -/
  φ : OY ⟶ O.obj
  /-- The sheaf module of differentials `Ω_{X/Y}` (a genuine sheaf of modules). -/
  Ω : SheafOfModules.{v} (ringSheaf O)
  /-- The universal `Y`-derivation `d_{X/Y} : O_X ⟶ Ω_{X/Y}`. -/
  d : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' Ω.val φ
  /-- `d_{X/Y}` is universal (Tag 04BN): the Stacks definition (Tag 04BL) of
  `Ω_{X/Y}` as the object representing the functor of `Y`-derivations. -/
  universal : d.Universal

attribute [instance] RingedToposOverBase.cat RingedToposOverBase.hsc

namespace RingedToposOverBase

variable (X : RingedToposOverBase.{v, u})

/-- The sheaf of rings `O_X` viewed in `RingCat`. -/
noncomputable abbrev ringSheaf' : Sheaf X.J RingCat.{u} := ringSheaf.{v, u} X.O

end RingedToposOverBase

/-- A **morphism of ringed topoi over the base diagram** `f : X' ⟶ X` together
with the data witnessing the commutative square
```
        f
   X' -----> X
   |         |
   v         v
   Y' -----> Y .
```
The data consists of:

* a continuous functor `Ff : C_X ⥤ C_X'` (the underlying continuous map of
  sites, inducing the inverse-image / direct-image functors on sheaves);
* the structure map `fsharp : O_X ⟶ f_* O_{X'}` of `f` (a homomorphism of
  sheaves of rings, equivalently `f⁻¹ O_X ⟶ O_{X'}` by the `f_* ⊣ f⁻¹`
  adjunction);
* the instance that the module pushforward along `fsharp` is a right adjoint,
  providing the genuine pullback `f^*` of sheaves of modules and the adjunction
  `f^* ⊣ f_*` (`SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction`);
* `fsharpY : g_X⁻¹ O_Y ⟶ Ff.op ⋙ (g_{X'}⁻¹ O_{Y'})`, the inverse image of the
  `Y`-structure factoring through the `Y'`-structure (coming from the bottom map
  `Y' ⟶ Y`), together with the commutativity hypothesis `hcomm` expressing that
  the square of structure sheaves commutes.  This is exactly the content "the
  two morphisms `X' ⟶ Y` agree", used in the Stacks proof to ensure the
  composite `D` annihilates `O_Y`. -/
structure MorphismOverBase (X' X : RingedToposOverBase.{v, u}) where
  /-- The underlying continuous functor of sites `C_X ⥤ C_X'`. -/
  Ff : X.C ⥤ X'.C
  /-- `Ff` is continuous for the topologies (so it induces functors on sheaves). -/
  [continuous : Ff.IsContinuous X.J X'.J]
  /-- The structure map `f♯ : O_X ⟶ f_* O_{X'}` (sheaves of rings). -/
  fsharp : X.ringSheaf' ⟶ (Ff.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} X.J X'.J).obj X'.ringSheaf'
  /-- The pushforward of modules along `f♯` is a right adjoint (so the pullback
  `f^*` and the adjunction `f^* ⊣ f_*` exist). -/
  [isRightAdjoint : (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{v} fsharp).IsRightAdjoint]
  /-- The inverse image of the `Y`-structure of `X`, factoring through the
  `Y'`-structure of `X'` (the bottom map `Y' ⟶ Y` of the square). -/
  fsharpY : X.OY ⟶ Ff.op ⋙ X'.OY
  /-- Commutativity of the square of structure sheaves: `φ_X ≫ f♯` agrees with
  `f♯_Y ≫ (Ff.op ⋙ φ_{X'})`.  Equivalently, the two morphisms `X' ⟶ Y` (via `X`
  and via `Y'`) coincide. -/
  hcomm :
    Functor.whiskerRight X.φ (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}) ≫
        (sheafToPresheaf X.J RingCat.{u}).map fsharp =
      Functor.whiskerRight fsharpY (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}) ≫
        Functor.whiskerLeft Ff.op
          (Functor.whiskerRight X'.φ (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}))

attribute [instance] MorphismOverBase.continuous MorphismOverBase.isRightAdjoint

namespace MorphismOverBase

variable {X' X : RingedToposOverBase.{v, u}} (f : MorphismOverBase X' X)

/-- The pushforward `f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}`, a sheaf of `O_X`-modules via `f♯`. -/
noncomputable abbrev pushΩ : SheafOfModules.{v} X.ringSheaf' :=
  (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{v} f.fsharp).obj X'.Ω

/-- The pullback `f^* Ω_{X/Y}`, a sheaf of `O_{X'}`-modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev pullΩ : SheafOfModules.{v} X'.ringSheaf' :=
  (SheafOfModules.pullback.{v} f.fsharp).obj X.Ω

/-- The `f^* ⊣ f_*` adjunction on sheaves of modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev adj :
    SheafOfModules.pullback.{v} f.fsharp ⊣ SheafOfModules.pushforward.{v} f.fsharp :=
  SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} f.fsharp

/-- The action of `f♯` on local sections: the ring homomorphism
`O_X(U) ⟶ O_{X'}(Ff U)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev fsharpApp (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    (X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U) →+* (X'.ringSheaf'.obj.obj (f.Ff.op.obj U)) :=
  (((sheafToPresheaf X.J RingCat.{u}).map f.fsharp).app U).hom

/-- The pulled-back universal local section `f^* d_{X/Y}(t)`.

For a local section `t ∈ O_X(U)`, the section `d_{X/Y}(t) ∈ Ω_{X/Y}(U)` is mapped
by the unit `η : Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ f_* f^* Ω_{X/Y}` of the adjunction `f^* ⊣ f_*` to a
section of `(f_* f^* Ω_{X/Y})(U) = (f^* Ω_{X/Y})(Ff U)`.  This is exactly the
local section `f^* d_{X/Y}(t)` of `f^* Ω_{X/Y}` from Statement 3 of
the source (the image of the generator `d_{X/Y}(t)` under `1 ⊗ id`). -/
noncomputable abbrev pullbackDiff (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (t : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U) :
    (f.pullΩ).val.obj (f.Ff.op.obj U) :=
  (((f.adj).unit.app X.Ω).val.app U).hom (X.d.d t)

end MorphismOverBase

/-!
## Main Statement(s)

We fix a morphism `f : X' ⟶ X` of ringed topoi over the base, i.e. a commutative
square as above (Stacks Tag 04BR).
-/

variable {X' X : RingedToposOverBase.{v, u}} (f : MorphismOverBase X' X)

/--
**Statement 1 (the composite is a `Y`-derivation).**

The composite map of sheaves of abelian groups on `Sh(C_X)`
`D := f_* d_{X'/Y'} ∘ f♯ : O_X ⟶ f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}`, given on local sections by
`a ↦ d_{X'/Y'}(f♯ a)`, is a `Y`-derivation `O_X ⟶ f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}` (where
`f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}` is the `O_X`-module via `f♯`).

We assert this by producing a genuine derivation `D` of the sheaf of modules
`f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}` (relative to `φ_X = g_X♯`) whose value on every local section
`a ∈ O_X(U)` is `d_{X'/Y'}(f♯ a)`.  Being a derivation packages additivity, the
Leibniz rule (which holds because `f♯` is a ring map and `d_{X'/Y'}` is a
derivation) and naturality; the annihilation of the image of the `Y`-structure
uses the commutativity `f.hcomm` of the square. -/
theorem statement1_isDerivation :
    ∃ D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (f.pushΩ).val X.φ,
      ∀ (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (a : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U),
        (D.app U).d a = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U a) := by
  refine ⟨{ d := fun {U} => (AddMonoidHom.mk'
              (fun a => (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U a))
              (fun a b => by
                show (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U (a + b))
                  = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U a)
                    + (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U b)
                rw [map_add (f.fsharpApp U)]
                exact map_add _ _ _) :
                (X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U) →+ f.pushΩ.val.obj U)
            d_mul := ?_
            d_map := ?_
            d_app := ?_ }, ?_⟩
  · intro U a b
    simp only [AddMonoidHom.mk'_apply, map_mul]
    rw [(X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d_mul]
    rfl
  · intro U V g x
    simp only [AddMonoidHom.mk'_apply]
    have nat := congrFun (congrArg (fun φ => φ.hom)
      (((sheafToPresheaf X.J RingCat).map f.fsharp).naturality g)) x
    simp only [RingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply] at nat
    have key : f.fsharpApp V (X.ringSheaf'.obj.map g x)
        = X'.ringSheaf'.obj.map (f.Ff.op.map g) (f.fsharpApp U x) := nat
    show (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj V)).d (f.fsharpApp V (X.ringSheaf'.obj.map g x))
      = (f.pushΩ.val.map g) ((X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U x))
    rw [key]
    exact X'.d.d_map (f.Ff.op.map g) (f.fsharpApp U x)
  · intro U s
    simp only [AddMonoidHom.mk'_apply]
    have hc := congrArg (fun η => (η.app U).hom s) f.hcomm
    simp only [Functor.whiskerRight_app, Functor.whiskerLeft_app,
      NatTrans.comp_app, RingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply] at hc
    have key : f.fsharpApp U (X.φ.app U s)
        = X'.φ.app (f.Ff.op.obj U) (f.fsharpY.app U s) := hc
    show (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U (X.φ.app U s)) = 0
    rw [key]
    exact ModuleCat.Derivation.d_map (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)) (f.fsharpY.app U s)
  · exact fun _ _ => rfl

/--
**Statement 2 (existence and uniqueness of the canonical maps `c'_f` and `c_f`).**

By the universal property of `Ω_{X/Y}` applied to the `Y`-derivation `D` of
Statement 1, there is a **unique** `O_X`-linear map
`c'_f : Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}` with `c'_f ∘ d_{X/Y} = D`, equivalently
`c'_f (d_{X/Y} t) = d_{X'/Y'}(f♯ t)` for every local section `t`.  Via the
`f^* ⊣ f_*` adjunction this corresponds to a canonical `O_{X'}`-linear map
`c_f : f^* Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}`, with `c'_f = (adjunction transpose of) c_f`. -/
theorem statement2_existence
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (f.pushΩ).val X.φ) :
    ∃! cf' : X.Ω ⟶ f.pushΩ, X.d.postcomp (SheafOfModules.forget _ |>.map cf') = D := by
  refine ⟨(SheafOfModules.forget _).preimage (X.universal.desc D), ?_, ?_⟩
  · simpa only [Functor.map_preimage] using X.universal.fac D
  · intro g hg
    apply (SheafOfModules.forget _).map_injective
    simp only [Functor.map_preimage]
    apply X.universal.postcomp_injective
    rw [X.universal.fac D, hg]

/--
**Statement 2, adjoint comparison map `c_f`.**

The unique map `c'_f : Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ f_* Ω_{X'/Y'}` of Statement 2 corresponds,
under the `f^* ⊣ f_*` adjunction on sheaves of modules, to the canonical
`O_{X'}`-linear comparison map `c_f : f^* Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}`. -/
theorem statement2_adjoint
    (cf' : X.Ω ⟶ f.pushΩ) :
    ∃! cf : f.pullΩ ⟶ X'.Ω, (f.adj).homEquiv X.Ω X'.Ω cf = cf' := by
  exact (f.adj.homEquiv X.Ω X'.Ω).bijective.existsUnique cf'

/--
**Statement 3, equivalence of the two characterizations.**

The direct local-section equation on `c_f` from `statement3_unique`
(`c_f ∘ (f^* d_{X/Y}(t)) = d_{X'/Y'}(f^* t)`) is equivalent to the
universal-property equation `c'_f ∘ d_{X/Y} = D` for the adjoint transpose
`c'_f = homEquiv c_f` (where `D` is the `Y`-derivation of Statement 1).  This is
exactly the content of the notational-abuse correction above: the
`f⁻¹ h_U^#` equation and the universal-property equation determine the same map. -/
theorem statement3_localSection_iff
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (f.pushΩ).val X.φ)
    (hD : ∀ (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (a : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U),
      (D.app U).d a = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U a))
    (cf : f.pullΩ ⟶ X'.Ω)
    (cf' : X.Ω ⟶ f.pushΩ)
    (hadj : (f.adj).homEquiv X.Ω X'.Ω cf = cf') :
    (∀ (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (t : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U),
        (cf.val.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).hom (f.pullbackDiff U t)
          = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U t))
      ↔ X.d.postcomp (SheafOfModules.forget _ |>.map cf') = D := by
  have key : ∀ (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (t : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U),
      (cf'.val.app U).hom (X.d.d t)
        = (cf.val.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).hom (f.pullbackDiff U t) := by
    intro U t
    subst hadj
    rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit]
    show (((SheafOfModules.pushforward f.fsharp).map cf).val.app U).hom
        (((f.adj.unit.app X.Ω).val.app U).hom (X.d.d t))
      = (cf.val.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).hom (f.pullbackDiff U t)
    rw [SheafOfModules.pushforward_map_val]
    exact PresheafOfModules.pushforward_map_app_apply f.fsharp.hom cf.val U _
  rw [SheafOfModules.forget_map]
  refine ⟨fun hP => ?_, fun hQ U t => ?_⟩
  · apply PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation.ext
    funext U
    apply AddMonoidHom.ext
    intro t
    show (cf'.val.app U).hom (X.d.d t) = D.d t
    rw [key U t, hP U t]
    exact (hD U t).symm
  · rw [← key U t]
    show (X.d.postcomp cf'.val).d t = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U t)
    rw [hQ]
    exact hD U t

/--
**Statement 3 (characterization and uniqueness of `c_f`).**

The comparison map `c_f : f^* Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}` is *uniquely* characterized by
the local-section property of Statement 3 (corrected
formulation):
`c_f ∘ (f^* d_{X/Y}(t)) = d_{X'/Y'} ∘ (f^* t)` as maps `f⁻¹ h_U^# ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}`.

We state this directly in terms of `c_f` (not its adjoint transpose): for every
object `U` and every local section `t ∈ O_X(U)`, `c_f` sends the pulled-back
universal section `f^* d_{X/Y}(t)` (the image of `d_{X/Y}(t)` under the
adjunction unit, i.e. `MorphismOverBase.pullbackDiff`, lying in
`(f^* Ω_{X/Y})(Ff U)`) to `d_{X'/Y'}(f♯ t)` (the local section
`d_{X'/Y'} ∘ (f^* t)` evaluated at `Ff U`).  Here `c_f` acts via its component
`c_f.val.app (Ff U) : (f^* Ω_{X/Y})(Ff U) ⟶ Ω_{X'/Y'}(Ff U)`, so the left-hand
side is literally `c_f` composed with the pulled-back section `f^* d_{X/Y}(t)`.

Uniqueness holds because the local sections `d_{X/Y}(t)` generate `Ω_{X/Y}` as an
`O_X`-module, so the sections `f^* d_{X/Y}(t)` generate `f^* Ω_{X/Y}` as an
`O_{X'}`-module (Stacks Tag 04BR). -/
@[stacks 04BR, ega "0 20.5.2" "(20.5.2.4) & (20.5.2.6)", ega "IV 16.4.3" "(16.4.3.6),(16.4.3.7)"]
theorem statement3_unique :
    ∃! cf : f.pullΩ ⟶ X'.Ω,
      ∀ (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (t : X.ringSheaf'.obj.obj U),
        (cf.val.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).hom (f.pullbackDiff U t)
          = (X'.d.app (f.Ff.op.obj U)).d (f.fsharpApp U t) := by
  obtain ⟨D, hD⟩ := statement1_isDerivation f
  obtain ⟨cf', hcf', hcf'uniq⟩ := statement2_existence f D
  set e := f.adj.homEquiv X.Ω X'.Ω
  refine ⟨e.symm cf', ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact (statement3_localSection_iff f D hD (e.symm cf') cf'
            (e.apply_symm_apply cf')).2 hcf'
  · intro cg hcg
    exact e.eq_symm_apply.2
      (hcf'uniq _ ((statement3_localSection_iff f D hD cg (e cg) rfl).1 hcg))

end Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials
